/-!
# Composed positive exact-one geometry profiles

The fifteen profiles describe zero through three source literal positions with every polarity
pattern. The coordinates compose the parsimonious disjunction, positive complement and forced
false gadgets. Every table matches the actual positive clause compiler, including its clause
order, variable names and auxiliary occurrences. Source terminals have one internal incidence;
the global drawing compiler removes their placeholder positions and joins their accesses to
the inherited source incidence routes.

## Main definitions

* `profileSource`, `profileFormula`, `profileVariables`: the exact logical profile.
* `profileGeometry`: its fixed orthogonal replacement data.

## References

The logical gadgets are from [HuntMaratheRadhakrishnanStearns1998, Theorem 3.8].
The coordinates and finite profiles are original.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Cslib.Complexity.SAT.ExactOne

open Cslib.Logic.PL Orthogonal

/-- Fifteen signed source clauses: every sign pattern on zero through three distinct slots. -/
abbrev ClauseProfile := Fin 15

/-- The signed source clause of a fixed profile, with variables named by their positions. -/
def profileSource (p : ClauseProfile) : Clause ℕ :=
  match p.val with
  | 0 => []
  | 1 => [(0, false)]
  | 2 => [(0, true)]
  | 3 => [(0, false), (1, false)]
  | 4 => [(0, false), (1, true)]
  | 5 => [(0, true), (1, false)]
  | 6 => [(0, true), (1, true)]
  | 7 => [(0, false), (1, false), (2, false)]
  | 8 => [(0, false), (1, false), (2, true)]
  | 9 => [(0, false), (1, true), (2, false)]
  | 10 => [(0, false), (1, true), (2, true)]
  | 11 => [(0, true), (1, false), (2, false)]
  | 12 => [(0, true), (1, false), (2, true)]
  | 13 => [(0, true), (1, true), (2, false)]
  | 14 => [(0, true), (1, true), (2, true)]
  | _ => []

/-- The actual composed logical compiler on one source profile. -/
def profileFormula (p : ClauseProfile) : CNF (CNF.PositiveExactOneCompile.Variable ℕ) :=
  CNF.PositiveExactOne.formula (CNF.FromSAT.clause 0 (profileSource p))

/-- The distinct logical variables, in the same order as the profile's variable positions. -/
def profileVariables (p : ClauseProfile) : List (CNF.PositiveExactOneCompile.Variable ℕ) :=
  (profileFormula p).distinctVars

